spec:
  id: domains
  version: 1.0.0
  status: stable
  priority: critical
  module: Ontology
  compiler_stage: Knowledge Representation
  description: >
purpose: Build a complete semantic map of software engineering.
philosophy[11]: Domains are not folders.,Domains represent engineering ecosystems.,"Every domain has:",Knowledge,Capabilities,Mental Models,Constraints,Artifacts,Tradeoffs,Failure Modes,Engineering Practices
hierarchy[9]: Domain,→,Subdomain,→,Topic,→,Concept,→,Knowledge Atom
domains:
  Foundations:
    purpose[2]: Mathematical and theoretical foundations,of computer science.
    concepts[6]: Mathematics,Logic,Set Theory,Information Theory,Complexity Theory,Computation Theory
  Programming:
    purpose[2]: Express computation using programming,languages.
    concepts[8]: Syntax,Semantics,Type Systems,Variables,Functions,Memory Models,Modules,Packages
  Algorithms:
    purpose: Efficient problem solving.
    concepts[7]: Searching,Sorting,Dynamic Programming,Greedy,Graph Algorithms,String Algorithms,Approximation
  Data_Structures:
    purpose: Organize information efficiently.
    concepts[7]: Arrays,Linked Lists,Trees,Graphs,Hash Tables,Heaps,Tries
  Operating_Systems:
    purpose: Resource management and execution.
    concepts[7]: Processes,Threads,Scheduling,Virtual Memory,Synchronization,Filesystems,IPC
  Compilers:
    purpose: Translate and optimize programs.
    concepts[7]: Lexing,Parsing,AST,Intermediate Representation,Optimization,Register Allocation,Linking
  Networking:
    purpose: Communication between systems.
    concepts[7]: TCP,UDP,HTTP,DNS,Routing,TLS,RPC
  Databases:
    purpose: Persistent storage and retrieval.
    concepts[7]: SQL,NoSQL,Transactions,ACID,CAP,Indexes,Query Planning
  Distributed_Systems:
    purpose: Coordinate computation across machines.
    concepts[6]: Consensus,Replication,Fault Tolerance,Distributed Storage,Messaging,Event Sourcing
  Security:
    purpose[2]: "Protect confidentiality,",integrity and availability.
    concepts[6]: Authentication,Authorization,Cryptography,Threat Modeling,Vulnerability Analysis,Secure Design
  Software_Architecture:
    purpose: Design maintainable and scalable systems.
    concepts[6]: Layers,Components,Microservices,Event Driven Architecture,CQRS,Design Patterns
  Testing:
    purpose: Verify engineering correctness.
    concepts[6]: Unit Tests,Integration Tests,Property Tests,Fuzzing,Mutation Testing,Benchmarks
  DevOps:
    purpose: Deliver reliable software continuously.
    concepts[7]: CI,CD,Containers,Kubernetes,Infrastructure,Monitoring,Deployment
  Performance:
    purpose: Maximize efficiency.
    concepts[6]: Profiling,Benchmarking,Optimization,Caching,SIMD,Parallelism
  Cloud:
    purpose: Distributed infrastructure.
    concepts[6]: Compute,Storage,Networking,IAM,Serverless,Multi Cloud
  AI_Engineering:
    purpose: Engineering intelligent systems.
    concepts[7]: ML,Deep Learning,LLMs,Agents,RAG,Fine Tuning,Evaluation
  Human_Factors:
    purpose: Engineering through collaboration.
    concepts[6]: Communication,Mentoring,Leadership,Documentation,Planning,Estimation
  Production_Engineering:
    purpose: Operate real-world software safely.
    concepts[6]: Monitoring,Alerting,Incident Response,SRE,Reliability,Observability
relationships[30]: Programming,→,Compilers,Programming,→,Operating_Systems,Algorithms,→,Data_Structures,Operating_Systems,→,Distributed_Systems,Networking,→,Distributed_Systems,Databases,→,Distributed_Systems,Software_Architecture,→,DevOps,DevOps,→,Production_Engineering,AI_Engineering,→,Distributed_Systems,Performance,→,Operating_Systems
cross_domain[9]: Debugging,Optimization,Design,Architecture,Documentation,Testing,Review,Communication,Learning
attributes[6]: maturity,complexity,abstraction_level,prerequisite_domains,engineering_density,reasoning_density
dependencies[11]: Foundations,→,Programming,→,Algorithms,→,Data_Structures,→,Systems,→,Distributed Systems
validation[5]: every_domain_has_purpose,every_domain_has_concepts,every_domain_connected,no_duplicate_domains,explicit_dependencies
requirements[9]: Purpose,Scope,Concepts,Capabilities,Constraints,Artifacts,Tradeoffs,Failure Modes,Related Domains
success[4]: Every engineering concept belongs to,exactly one primary domain.,Every domain forms a coherent ecosystem.,Cross-domain reasoning is explicit.
guarantees[5]: Complete engineering coverage.,Domain independence.,Explicit relationships.,Extensible hierarchy.,Deterministic classification.
future:
  unlimited_domains: true
  evolving_relationships: true
  dynamic_dependencies: true
  graph_embeddings: true
  adaptive_curriculum: true
